Upstream-Status: Inappropriate

Subject: [PATCH] x86/mm: Give no process a global ASID with isolcpus=noasid

A process gets a global ASID when one of its flushes finds it active on
four or more CPUs, and from then on its TLB flushes are INVLPGB
broadcasts: every CPU in the system, isolated ones included, takes the
invalidation, and the flushing CPU waits in TLBSYNC for all of them
(twice on CPUs with erratum #1718).  isolcpus=asid keeps the processes
that run only on housekeeping CPUs off this path, but a process that
also runs on isolated CPUs keeps it, and each of its flushes reaches all
the other isolated CPUs, those that run other processes among them,
without an interrupt to count.

With isolcpus=noasid no process gets a global ASID: its flushes are IPIs
to the CPUs that have it loaded (and, at most once a second, to the
stale CPUs of its mm_cpumask()), never to the CPUs of other processes.
The cost falls on the process itself: one that flushes while it runs on
isolated CPUs now interrupts them, where the broadcast did not.  Kernel
flushes and the batched flushes of reclaim and migration keep using
INVLPGB.
---
--- a/include/linux/sched/isolation.h
+++ b/include/linux/sched/isolation.h
@@ -34,6 +34,7 @@
 	ISOL_STRICT_PSI,
 	ISOL_STRICT_ASID,
 	ISOL_STRICT_NODE,
+	ISOL_STRICT_NOASID,
 	ISOL_STRICT_MAX
 };
 
--- a/kernel/sched/isolation.c
+++ b/kernel/sched/isolation.c
@@ -30,6 +30,7 @@
 nodemask_t isolcpus_strict_nodes __ro_after_init;
 
 static const char * const isolcpus_strict_names[ISOL_STRICT_MAX] = {
+	[ISOL_STRICT_NOASID]	= "noasid",
 	[ISOL_STRICT_NODE]	= "node",
 	[ISOL_STRICT_ASID]	= "asid",
 	[ISOL_STRICT_PSI]	= "psi",
--- a/arch/x86/mm/tlb.c
+++ b/arch/x86/mm/tlb.c
@@ -448,6 +448,15 @@
 	if (!cpu_feature_enabled(X86_FEATURE_INVLPGB))
 		return;
 
+	/*
+	 * With isolcpus=noasid, no process gets a global ASID: its flushes go
+	 * by IPI to the CPUs in its mm_cpumask(), the ones that run it, and
+	 * not by a broadcast INVLPGB that every CPU in the system has to take,
+	 * including those that run other processes.
+	 */
+	if (isolcpus_strict_enabled(ISOL_STRICT_NOASID))
+		return;
+
 	/* Check every once in a while. */
 	if ((current->pid & 0x1f) != (jiffies & 0x1f))
 		return;
